  "applicability_scope": [
    "Level 1 review by Shuangping Li on 12 November 2026 of the P22 arXiv v2 Results/Overview.lean statements of Theorems 4.1, 5.1, 6.1, 6.6, and 7.3, with AI-assisted statement translations.",
    "Theorem 4.1: uniform generation and uniform generation with replay are equivalent at every fixed positive sample threshold, without a UUS assumption.",
    "Theorem 5.1: the explicit class nonuniformHardClass on Sum Nat Nat, support-isomorphic to the source's nonzero integers, is non-uniformly generatable but not non-uniformly generatable with replay.",
    "Theorem 6.1: semantic replay generation in the limit for every indexed infinite-language oracle family over a countable domain, and on the normalized Nat universe a single carried-cutoff Witness Protection generator whose every round is determined by a valid finite answered-query cache.",
    "Theorem 6.6: an uncountable UUS class on Sum Int Nat generatable in the limit but not generatable in the limit with replay.",
    "Theorem 7.3: a four-member family of infinite integer languages that is not properly generatable in the limit with replay.",
    "Recursive project-local statement-relevant definitions, including the replay sequence and enumeration predicates, proper-generation predicates, indexed oracle families, and the Witness Protection state, run, and finite-query-trace definitions named by the finite-query form of Theorem 6.1.",
    "Supporting proof-certificate types guard the meaning of definitions only; they are not separate human audit claims."
  ],
